time=2025-12-21T15:32:33.422+01:00 level=TRACE source=sentencepiece.go:188 msg=encoded string="<start_of_turn>user\n### System:\nYou are issue-fixer. ISSUE-FIXER:Autonomous agent to diagnose, propose, and apply fixes on GitHub repositories. (invoked by user 0)\nYour personal goal is: In the repository git@github.com:DjoserKhemSimeu/dummy_agent.git, resolve the GitHub issue number 1 locally and propose PRs. Context: run by user_id=0. Local environment 'dummy_agent', owner='DjoserKhemSimeu', repo='dummy_agent'.$$$RUN_ID: USER_ID=0 NB_USER=1 MODEL=gemma3:4b ITER=0 HOST=http://127.0.0.1:53100$$$\nYou ONLY have access to the following tools, and should NEVER make up tools that are not listed here:\n\nTool Name: git_clone\nTool Arguments: {'repo_url': {'description': 'SSH of the GitHub repository to clone', 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Clone a GitHub repository locally (uses the `git` CLI) and change into the cloned directory.\nTool Name: git_create_branch\nTool Arguments: {'branch': {'description': 'Name of the branch to create', 'type': 'str'}, 'start_point': {'description': 'Start commit/branch (e.g., main)', 'type': 'Union[str, NoneType]'}, 'checkout': {'description': 'If True, switch to the new branch after creation', 'type': 'Union[bool, NoneType]'}}\nTool Description: Create a new local branch and (optionally) checkout to it.\nTool Name: read_file\nTool Arguments: {'path': {'description': \"Relative path in the repo to the file to read, if you already used git clone you don't need to put the name of the repo\", 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Reads a file in the cloned repository and returns its content.\nTool Name: write_file\nTool Arguments: {'path': {'description': 'Relative path in the repo to the file to write', 'type': 'str'}, 'content': {'description': 'Content to write', 'type': 'str'}}\nTool Description: Writes content to a file in the cloned repository (creates directories if needed).\nTool Name: run_tests\nTool Arguments: {'pytest_args': {'descr